      "text": "To find the first digit of the base 8 representation of \\(473_{10}\\), we need to convert the decimal number 473 to its base 8 (octal) form. The first step in this conversion is to determine how many octal digits are needed to represent 473. We do this by finding the largest power of 8 that is less than or equal to 473.\n\nThe powers of 8 are:\n\\[8^0 = 1\\]\n\\[8^1 = 8\\]\n\\[8^2 = 64\\]\n\\[8^3 = 512\\]\n\\[8^4 = 4096\\] (which is greater than 473, so we don't need higher powers)\n\nSince \\(8^3 = 512\\) is greater than 473 and \\(8^2 = 64\\) is less than 473, we use \\(8^3\\) and \\(8^2\\).\n\nFirst, we calculate how many times \\(8^3\\) fits into 473:\n\\[473 \\div 512 \\approx 0.92\\] (so, the coefficient of \\(8^3\\) is 0)\n\nNext, we calculate how many times \\(8^2\\) fits into the remainder:\n\\[473 - 0 \\cdot 512 = 473\\]\n\\[473 \\div 64 = 7.33\\] (so, the coefficient of \\(8^2\\) is 7)\n\nNow, we calculate how many times \\(8^1\\) fits into the remainder:\n\\[473 - 7 \\cdot 64 = 473 - 448 = 25\\]\n\\[25 \\div 8 = 3.125\\] (so, the coefficient of \\(8^1\\) is 3)\n\nFinally, the coefficient of \\(8^0\\) is 2.\n\nPutting it all together, the base 8 representation of 473 is \\(732_8\\). The first digit from left to right is 7. Therefore, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]",
