      "text": "To find the first digit of the base \\( 8 \\) representation of \\( 473_{10} \\), we'll convert \\( 473_{10} \\) to base \\( 8 \\) step by step. To convert a decimal number \\( n \\) to base \\( b \\), we repeatedly divide \\( n \\) by \\( b \\) and keep track of the remainders.\n\nLet's denote the base \\( 8 \\) representation of \\( 473_{10} \\) as \\( d_k d_{k-1} \\ldots d_1 d_0 \\ldots \\), where each \\( d_i \\) is the digit in the \\( i \\)-th position.\n\nWe'll perform the following steps:\n\n1. **Initialize variables:**\n   - Start with \\( n = 473 \\).\n   - Initialize the list of remainders to store each digit in base \\( 8 \\).\n\n2. **Repeated division:**\n   - Divide \\( n \\) by \\( 8 \\) and record the remainder.\n   - Update \\( n \\) with the quotient from the division.\n\n3. **While \\( n \\) is greater than \\( 0 \\):**\n   - Continue the division and record the remainder.\n   - Update \\( n \\) with the quotient from each division.\n\n4. **Determine the first digit:**\n   - The first digit is the least significant digit in the list of remainders.\n\nLet’s implement this in Python to find the first digit of \\( 473_{10} \\) in base \\( 8 \\).\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_n(decimal_number, base):\n    if decimal_number == 0:\n        return '0'\n    digits = []\n    while decimal_number:\n        digits.append(int(decimal_number % base))\n        decimal_number //= base\n    return ''.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 473 from base 10 to base 8\nbase_8_representation = decimal_to_base_n(473, 8)\nfirst_digit = base_8_representation[0]\nprint((base_8_representation, first_digit))\n```\n```output\n('631', '6')\n```\nThe base \\( 8 \\) representation of \\( 473_{10} \\) is \\( 631_8 \\). \n\nThe first digit of this base \\( 8 \\) representation is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
