      "text": "To determine the first digit of the base $8$ representation of the decimal number $473_{10}$, we need to convert $473_{10}$ to its base $8$ equivalent. This can be done by repeatedly dividing the number by $8$ and keeping track of the remainders.\n\nLet's go through the steps:\n\n1. Divide $473$ by $8$:\n   \\[\n   473 \\div 8 = 59 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n   \\]\n   So, the least significant digit (rightmost) of the base $8$ representation is $1$.\n\n2. Divide the quotient $59$ by $8$:\n   \\[\n   59 \\div 8 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 3\n   \\]\n   So, the next digit in base $8$ is $3$.\n\n3. Divide the quotient $7$ by $8$:\n   \\[\n   7 \\div 8 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 7\n   \\]\n   So, the next digit in base $8$ is $7$.\n\nSince the quotient is now $0$, we stop the division process. Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ as $731_8$.\n\nThe first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $7$. Therefore, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]",
